 34AR    COULOMB EXCITATION:XUNDL-6    2023DR01                           202308
 34AR c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2023Dr01: Phys. Rev.C 107, 034306  
 34AR2c  (2023).                                                                
 34AR c  Compiled by G. G~urdal, Apr 13, 2023                                   
 34AR c  An intermediate Coulomb excitation experiment was performed to         
 34AR2c  measure the B(E2, 0{++}{-1} |) 2{++}{-1}) value of {+36,38}Ca.         
 34AR3c  {+34}Ar beam was a contaminant produced from the                       
 34AR4c  fragmentation of a 140 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca primary beam delivered by   
 34AR5c  the Coupled Cyclotron Facility at the National Superconducting         
 34AR6c  Cyclotron Laboratory (NSCL) impinging upon an 800 mg/cm{+2} thick      
 34AR7c  {+9}Be production target and separated using a 300 mg/cm{+2} Al wedge  
 34AR8c  degrader in the A1900 fragment separator. Secondary                    
 34AR9c  beam was scattered off a 257 mg/cm{++2} thick Au foil located at the   
 34ARac  target position of the S800 spectrograph. The deexcited |g-rays were   
 34ARbc  detected using GRETINA surrounded S800 spectrograph. The GRETINA       
 34ARcc  consisted a total of 48 HPGe crystals; 32 of them at 90|' and 16 of    
 34ARdc  them at 58|' with respect to the beam direction. The inelastic         
 34ARec  excitations of the projectile and target nuclei were quantified with   
 34ARfc  the detection of prompt |g-rays in GRETINA. The scattered projectiles  
 34ARgc  were identified using S800 focal plane detection system together with  
 34ARhc  tof measurement. Measured: E|g, tof, cross section and B(E2).          
 34ARic  Comparison with the shell model calculations.                          
 34AR cL J$From the Adopted Levels of {+34}Ar in ENSDF database.                
 34AR cL E$From E|g                                                             
 34AR cG E$From Table I in 2023Dr01.                                            
